.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-DOWNLOAD-FILE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-download-file \- download an object from a bucket to a local file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm download-file
.BR \-\-bucket\-ern | \-b
.I ERN
.BR \-\-key | \-k
.I KEY
.BR \-\-file | \-f
.I PATH
[\fB\-\-part\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIBYTES\fR]
[\fB\-\-concurrency\fR|\fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads an object from a bucket to a local file. This is the mirror
image of
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1).
Since an object's size isn't known until asked (unlike a local file
being uploaded), a single-request fetch is always tried first; if the
object turns out to be at or above
.BR \-\-part\-size ,
the server rejects it and this transparently falls back to the
create-download/download-part/complete-download sequence instead, so
multipart download is invisible to the caller either way.
.PP
For a multipart download, the destination file is created and
pre-sized to the object's full length up front, then up to
.B \-\-concurrency
parts are downloaded in parallel in background threads, each one
written directly at its own byte offset - so parts can land in any
order without corrupting the file. Each part is retried a few times
with backoff on network failures or a server error (HTTP 5xx) before
the whole download is aborted; a rejected part (HTTP 4xx) is not
retried.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the source bucket. Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Key (path) of the object within the bucket. Required.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Local destination file. Overwritten if it already exists. Required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-part\-size " " \fIBYTES\fR
Size of each part, in bytes. Defaults to \fI5242880\fR (5 MiB), or the
value of \fIeuclid.modules.storage.part-size\fR in the loaded
configuration file if set - see
.BR \-\-config
in
.BR euclid-cli (1).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-concurrency " " \fIN\fR
Number of parts to download in parallel. Defaults to \fI4\fR, or the
value of \fIeuclid.modules.storage.concurrency\fR in the loaded
configuration file if set; values less than \fI1\fR are treated as
\fI1\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The file was downloaded. On the single-request path, a summary
.RI ( "{bucketErn, key, size, file}" )
is printed as JSON; on the multipart path, the full object metadata
.RI ( "{bucketErn, key, ern, size, contentType, file}" )
is printed instead.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the destination file could not be created,
no object with that bucket/key exists, the object is not yet fully
uploaded, or any part failed to download after retries.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm download-file \e
    --bucket-ern ern:euclid:storage:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --key 2026-08.csv --file ./2026-08.csv

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm download-file \e
    --bucket-ern ern:euclid:storage:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --key archive/2026-08.csv --file ./2026-08.csv \e
    --part-size 8388608 --concurrency 8
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-download-bucket (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-objects (1)
